# Stacking PRs rule (always apply)

Always enforced with the rest of `.cursor/rules/`.

1. **Prefer stacks over mega-PRs** when a change spans multiple concerns or exceeds layer budgets
2. Read [`skills/stacking-prs/SKILL.md`](../skills/stacking-prs/SKILL.md) before operating a stack
3. Tooling: GitHub stacked PRs + `gh stack` (docs); install `github/gh-stack`
4. Trunk = org integration base (`dev` here) unless hotfix → `main`
5. **Layer budgets** (vs parent branch):

| Metric | Target | Ceiling |
| ------ | ------ | ------- |
| Files | ≤20 | **30** |
| Net lines (excl. lock/gen when judging) | ≤300 | **500** |
| Themes / concerns | 1 | 1 |

6. Over ceiling → **split** (`gh stack add`) before `gh stack submit` — ⊥ ship oversized layer
7. Dependency order: foundation bottom · dependents above · never put deps above dependents
8. Fix on the owning layer → `gh stack rebase --upstack` → push; ⊥ silent force-push (AskQuestion)
9. Merge **bottom-up** (`gh stack merge` or UI); mid-merge re-targets above to trunk
10. Squash-into-trunk conflict artifact → skill [`reference.md`](../skills/stacking-prs/reference.md) § Squash sync (Pacheco)
11. Operate/sync/submit on **main thread** (or `ship-execute` under `/ship`) — no dedicated stacking agent
12. Same-repo only — cross-fork stacks unsupported

Concise **full**. Security / irreversible git → clear English first.
